       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem, and you've told me you aren't a clinician. A dose of 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin, and I can't verify that a prescriber has approved it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **The treating prescriber enters or co-signs the order.** If they intend this dose, they can document why and enter it themselves. Pharmacy will probably also want to review it.\n- **You give me a dose within the labeled range.** For example, I can enter metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) as soon as you or the prescriber confirm it.\n- **Pharmacy or the medical director reviews the order.** This works if there's a clinical reason for the higher dose.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter the order if it's a safe dose."
